=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
Full investigation of every component the ticket implicated found no fault. The DNS server (`dns_server`, IP 10.200.0.2) is running BIND9 (`named`) with a correctly loaded `local` zone that authoritatively resolves `web0.local` through `web3.local` to the correct server IPs (10.200.0.3–10.200.0.6). All four web servers (`web_server_0` through `web_server_3`) have Apache running and serving their respective index pages. Both host machines (`host_1_1_1_1` at 10.1.1.2 and `host_2_1_1_1` at 10.2.1.2) correctly use 10.200.0.2 as their resolver, DNS lookups complete in approximately 1–2 ms, and end-to-end HTTP GETs to `http://web0.local/` return HTTP 200 with the correct page in under 4 ms. The OSPF topology is fully converged: `router_core_1` and `router_core_2` act as ABRs bridging the backbone (area 0, containing the three core routers and the server-access switch) with area 1 (containing the distribution switches and host subnets). No iptables rules are blocking traffic on any device. The routing tables at every layer carry correct OSPF-learned paths. Root cause: there is no network fault — the helpdesk ticket cannot be reproduced. The network is healthy and the user's reported symptom is not substantiated by any diagnostic evidence gathered inside the lab.
=== END ===